  "name": "Call and Response Square",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "One bar, two phrases: a bouncing call of several barks, then a thinner answer that leaves a hole before the next downbeat. Play: hold F1, A#1 or G1 for a full bar-long riff from a single key, or stab it against a half-time kick at 140-150 BPM; the pattern restarts on every new note. Macros: Call Depth deepens the spectral jump on every hit, Response Gap fades the answer phrase out, Bite thins the body and Grit pushes the hard clip.",
